  "description": "BUKJOI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H134 Dy6 O38. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.732-3.819 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.44-113.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H134Dy6O38.",
